WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.508
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.508 --> 00:00:04.737
Today's message is be driven.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.654
Over to you Jamie Foxx.

00:00:09.432 --> 00:00:12.292
(rooster crows)

00:00:12.292 --> 00:00:14.818
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:18.741
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:20.692
- So I had to learn drive.

00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:23.630
That's why I have my
managers to teach me drive

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.470
or to, you know, push me
because you can relax.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.527
You could say, "Oh, I could do that"

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.469
or "I could do that."

00:00:28.469 --> 00:00:30.172
But, are you going to be that person?

00:00:30.172 --> 00:00:32.331
I know this person, this
person that calls me up,

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:35.461
"Man, did you see what
Denzel did in that movie?

00:00:35.461 --> 00:00:37.115
He said, "I could've."

00:00:37.115 --> 00:00:40.310
And, maybe he could have, but
he doesn't have the drive,

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:45.172
the Denzel, and so therefore,
if you don't have drive,

00:00:45.172 --> 00:00:47.865
you quit cultivating your talent,

00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:50.090
because once you rest, and
once you say it's over,

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:51.593
"I've gotten to the mountain top.",

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:53.241
then your talent starts to dwindle too.

00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:56.050
That's why the minute the
award season was over,

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.484
I was at Wet Willies in
Miami doing jokes for people

00:00:58.484 --> 00:01:01.293
just on the street, just
to see what would work,

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:02.659
you know, Jokes either about the Oscars,

00:01:02.659 --> 00:01:03.597
or jokes about whatever,

00:01:03.597 --> 00:01:06.630
and then you go to Atlanta
and work on your jokes there.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.357
So, that hustle, what I call
hustle, is very important

00:01:10.357 --> 00:01:12.981
because, at some point,
you're going to be able to

00:01:12.981 --> 00:01:14.637
pull the hustle back just a little bit,

00:01:14.637 --> 00:01:15.915
and then you pick your spots.

00:01:15.915 --> 00:01:17.957
The time right now is to
hustle to set things up

00:01:17.957 --> 00:01:21.423
so that in the future
you're able to cut back

00:01:21.423 --> 00:01:23.967
just a little bit, and
just pick your spots.

00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:26.096
- For me, a lot of this still
comes down to environment.

00:01:26.096 --> 00:01:28.691
I think the environment
that you're in matters.

00:01:28.691 --> 00:01:29.997
The people around you matters.

00:01:29.997 --> 00:01:32.270
Again, what you're reading,
what you watch really matters

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.747
because, I think, too many people

00:01:33.747 --> 00:01:35.314
are comfortable where they are,

00:01:35.314 --> 00:01:37.295
and their environment
keeps them where they are,

00:01:37.295 --> 00:01:39.487
and you don't have people
pushing you to get better,

00:01:39.487 --> 00:01:40.913
pushing you to drive faster,

00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:43.042
pushing you to go a little bit harder.

00:01:43.042 --> 00:01:44.916
I think a lot of people
are just comfortable

00:01:44.916 --> 00:01:46.679
being the big fish in the small pond,

00:01:46.679 --> 00:01:48.771
instead of jumping to a bigger pond

00:01:48.771 --> 00:01:50.739
and being that small fish
trying to get better.

00:01:50.739 --> 00:01:53.716
I think a lot of people
are in a race, you know.

00:01:53.716 --> 00:01:55.043
They're in a 100 Meter race,

00:01:55.043 --> 00:01:56.569
and they're racing against five year olds.

00:01:56.569 --> 00:01:57.965
So, they win all the time.

00:01:57.965 --> 00:02:00.435
And when you are winning all
the time, in that small race,

00:02:00.435 --> 00:02:02.495
it's easy to just stay there.

00:02:02.495 --> 00:02:04.374
"Look at me, I'm great.

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:05.631
"Look at all the great stuff I'm doing.

00:02:05.631 --> 00:02:07.073
"I don't need to work harder.

00:02:07.073 --> 00:02:08.677
"I don't need to push faster.

00:02:08.677 --> 00:02:10.158
"I'm already winning everything."

00:02:10.158 --> 00:02:13.346
And for a lot of people,
that's where they are.

00:02:13.346 --> 00:02:15.183
You know, that's where I was,

00:02:15.183 --> 00:02:19.106
where I was doing more
than the people around me,

00:02:19.106 --> 00:02:22.630
where anytime we'd have get
togethers, coffees, meetings,

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.569
or whatever, it was always only praise.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:26.753
Like, "Oh, look at this great
stuff that you're doing."

00:02:26.753 --> 00:02:28.122
And it's easy for me to sit back and say

00:02:28.122 --> 00:02:29.857
"Yeah, look at all this
great stuff I'm doing.",

00:02:29.857 --> 00:02:31.784
and take my foot off the gas.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.538
But I want to play in the bigger game.

00:02:33.538 --> 00:02:35.874
I want to race against Usain Bolt.

00:02:35.874 --> 00:02:38.845
I want to race against people
who are faster than me.

00:02:38.845 --> 00:02:40.590
And I may lose.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.766
I'm going to lose racing
against Usain Bolt.

00:02:43.766 --> 00:02:46.569
I'm going to lose against
people who are faster than me.

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:48.902
But, my time will be faster.

00:02:50.072 --> 00:02:52.289
My time racing against
a five year old versus

00:02:52.289 --> 00:02:54.588
my time racing against sprinters,

00:02:54.588 --> 00:02:58.082
I may lose that race, but
my time will be faster.

00:02:58.082 --> 00:02:59.807
So I'm getting better.

00:02:59.807 --> 00:03:01.399
I'm pushing harder,

00:03:01.399 --> 00:03:03.647
and, so, that's what
you need for yourself.

00:03:03.647 --> 00:03:04.721
You want to be driven?

00:03:04.721 --> 00:03:05.955
You want to do something bigger?

00:03:05.955 --> 00:03:07.472
You want to push more?

00:03:07.472 --> 00:03:10.722
You need to have people around
you who are better than you.

00:03:10.722 --> 00:03:12.357
It's why I started the Top Ten Series

00:03:12.357 --> 00:03:15.029
and the Mentor Me Series,
to learn from people,

00:03:15.029 --> 00:03:17.208
to be around them, who've
done a lot more than us.

00:03:17.208 --> 00:03:19.993
So, I look at my life,
and while I'm grateful

00:03:19.993 --> 00:03:21.026
for everything that's happened,

00:03:21.026 --> 00:03:22.816
and everything that's been accomplished,

00:03:22.816 --> 00:03:25.543
I still realize that
it's nothing compared to

00:03:25.543 --> 00:03:27.574
what all these other people are doing.

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:28.800
It's not looking at
those people and saying,

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:29.665
"Well, I suck.

00:03:29.665 --> 00:03:30.645
"I can't go out and do that."

00:03:30.645 --> 00:03:31.592
It's inspiration.

00:03:31.592 --> 00:03:33.608
I can push harder.

00:03:33.608 --> 00:03:35.249
I'm not pushing hard enough right now.

00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:36.720
I can do more.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:37.607
I'm not just going to sit back

00:03:37.607 --> 00:03:39.005
and keep racing five year olds.

00:03:39.005 --> 00:03:41.165
I want to go off and play a bigger game.

00:03:41.165 --> 00:03:42.676
I want to jump to that bigger pool.

00:03:42.676 --> 00:03:44.846
So, if you're worried that
you're not driven enough,

00:03:44.846 --> 00:03:46.510
that you're not following
through on your goals enough,

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.644
that you don't have big enough goals,

00:03:47.644 --> 00:03:49.660
that you don't believe in yourself enough,

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.117
look at your environment.

00:03:52.117 --> 00:03:53.773
Look at your habits, look at your routine,

00:03:53.773 --> 00:03:54.812
look at the people around you.

00:03:54.812 --> 00:03:58.330
Look at what you're consuming
on a consistent daily basis.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.663
You need to be around people and things

00:04:00.663 --> 00:04:03.012
that push you to do more,

00:04:03.012 --> 00:04:05.703
to believe in yourself more,
to dream bigger dreams,

00:04:05.703 --> 00:04:07.090
to believe that those are possible,

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:10.560
to go and chase, to wake up
and work and hustle and drive,

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.685
for yourself, for your
family, for your community,

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:13.979
for the world, it's important.

00:04:13.979 --> 00:04:16.907
So, if you're on the
lazy side, chances are

00:04:16.907 --> 00:04:20.798
you have an environment around
you that supports laziness.

00:04:20.798 --> 00:04:23.939
Change your environment,
start changing your life.

00:04:23.939 --> 00:04:25.699
So the the question of the day today is,

00:04:25.699 --> 00:04:28.658
Do you have an environment
that supports you

00:04:28.658 --> 00:04:32.083
in accomplishing your big dreams, or not?

00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:33.208
Leave it in the comments below.

00:04:33.208 --> 00:04:34.622
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:04:34.622 --> 00:04:37.171
Also, I want to give a quick
shout out to Aurora Balogidi.

00:04:37.171 --> 00:04:39.222
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book.

00:04:39.222 --> 00:04:41.313
It really, really,
really means a lot to me,

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:43.704
and I hope it helps
you find your one word.

00:04:43.704 --> 00:04:45.317
So, thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.448
I believe in you.

00:04:46.448 --> 00:04:48.380
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.751
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:50.751 --> 00:04:52.900
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.324
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:55.324 --> 00:04:57.883
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:57.883 --> 00:05:01.159
♫ Entspresso keep me going

